WEBVTT

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:08.560
Here I come, Arashi-san.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:09.700
Bring it!

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:36.630
Got it!

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:53.120
Jun, why do you wear men's clothes, anyway?

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:58.700
I was modeling some male uniforms around here one time,

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:02.190
and during my break, I wore them to the Ark.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:05.140
Yasaka mistook me for a guy.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:09.750
Are you planning to keep secret from everyone that you're a girl?

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:11.810
I...

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:17.230
Arashi?

00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:18.280
Yasaka?

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:19.440
What are you doing?

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:54.380
Relationship to Others

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.960
I think it's a goner.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:00.200
Yeah...

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:05.500
It's been there for ages.
Kind of sad to think it'll be gone.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.510
Leave it to me, Arashi-san.

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:13.130
We need the weathervane there!

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.290
Why?

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:19.840
When we come to the Ark,
it's the first thing to greet us.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:24.280
Yeah, because we come up the hill.

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:31.500
When we see this, we know we're almost there

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.810
and use our final turbo boost on the bike!

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:40.980
So that's why you always pedal standing up, near the end.

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:43.120
I thought it was the steep incline.

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:44.340
No, that's part of it.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:49.250
If you get tired and partially put your feet on the ground, you're a failure as a man.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:50.450
Kid.

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:52.710
But I would be happy if you fixed it.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:56.550
It's watched over the place for years.

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:58.050
Watched over?

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:03.420
In addition to telling which way the wind blows, the weathervane wards off bad luck.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:09.430
Maybe it's thanks to this that the Ark wasn't destroyed during the air raids.

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:10.890
I see.

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:14.900
So, yeah! We need to have this here at the Ark.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:17.570
We're climbing up there, Kamigamo.
Time to prove ourselves as men!

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:18.870
Me, too?

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:21.520
N-N-No way!

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:22.640
I'm not going up there!

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:24.770
Come on, city boy.

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:27.400
We're guys. We have to do it.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:32.100
We can't let frail little Arashi-san and Kaya-san do something so dangerous.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.530
You say that, but...

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:36.910
It's just scary 'cause you're standing there freaking out about it.

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:37.470
Come on.

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:42.940
H-Hey, that's dangerous!

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:51.640
Man, it's nice.

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:55.580
That damn weathervane had this view all to himself.

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.260
Arashi-san!

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.450
You're the best!

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:03.430
Yasaka?

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:06.240
Arashi-san, you're wonderful!

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:09.780
Kamigamo, you try it, too.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:11.290
It feels good.

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:14.000
No. Why would I do something so pointless?

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.350
I don't have anything to yell, anyway.

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:18.940
Come on, just yell something.

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:20.120
What idiocy.

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:21.640
I'm not doing it.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:23.880
Just say what comes to mind.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.270
Scream it out.

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:27.910
Say what's bothering you.

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:30.170
It always makes me feel better.

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:32.090
I'll pass.

00:05:32.090 --> 00:05:33.620
Why not?

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:35.110
Next time.

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:36.980
Why "next time"?

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:42.920
If you don't say what you can now,
that's really pointless.

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:46.290
Listen. A man should speak his mind,

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:47.730
tell people right away!

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:52.630
You forgot that Arashi-san's down there, didn't you?

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:56.500
Hajime-chan, I can hear every word you say.

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:00.000
And you wait till now to tell me that?!

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:01.810
Idiot.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:07.030
Hey, a question.

00:06:07.490 --> 00:06:10.570
Where were you until last summer?

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:12.800
Why this, all of a sudden?

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:16.670
I was just thinking you could've come to the Ark much sooner.

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:22.150
Well, you know, the whole place reminds her of that wimp with the glasses.

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:23.220
Wimp?

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:25.860
A woman's heart is complicated.

00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:32.000
She dragged a kid into the middle of an air raid,
waving her maiden's heart around?

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:33.170
Scary!

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:37.710
Excuse me, pass the salt.

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:41.950
Arashi! I've told you so many times to keep your mouth shut about things!

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:45.490
Oh, come on. It was long, long ago.

00:06:45.490 --> 00:06:46.990
So, where were you?

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:51.220
Every summer, I was at Ookurayama, where the school is.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:55.310
I almost never came to Hakuraku.

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:59.760
But she knew about the weathervane, for all that.

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:02.150
Must've heard it from the wimp with the glasses...

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:04.470
You two!

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:14.700
Then maybe there are others like Arashi-san and Kaya-san who just haven't come here?

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:15.480
Well...

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:15.480
Salt...

00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:19.960
It's hard to believe, but I can't deny the possibility.

00:07:20.350 --> 00:07:22.370
What would they have in common?

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:27.780
The massive Yokohama air raid on May 29th, Showa 20.

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:30.840
The day we died and this resulted.

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:35.760
If we go there, we may find the answer to the mystery.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:38.460
Give it up.

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:40.530
You'll probably get killed.

00:07:40.530 --> 00:07:42.070
Fine by me!

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:43.770
You serious?

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:44.710
Of course.

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:47.550
I'll risk my life for the woman I love!

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:50.300
I'd really like to hit you.

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:53.870
I don't think it's that funny.

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:55.210
Kamigamo?

00:07:55.210 --> 00:08:00.700
I feel bad for Kaya-san, but I never want to go anywhere dangerous again.

00:08:03.070 --> 00:08:04.670
I'm going shopping.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:22.050
This is...

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:34.410
Jeez, why do I have to run their errands?

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:37.590
Damn, going in is hard.

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:47.300
Welcome.

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:50.500
Are you looking for something?

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:53.080
Um, well...

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:55.720
These aren't for me.

00:08:56.010 --> 00:08:57.830
But ya, I'd like, uh,

00:08:57.830 --> 00:08:59.080
magical, almost invisible p-

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:00.770
Panties?

00:09:03.970 --> 00:09:05.140
Give me these.

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:08.810
He's such a girl.

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:11.400
It's the sane reaction.

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:14.970
It makes sense.

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:16.510
Nobody would want that.

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:17.750
It's normal.

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:20.080
Excuse me, pass the salt.

00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:22.390
I'm fine with it,

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:23.330
Arashi-san!

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:26.750
Let's leave the wuss out of it and keep talking.

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:29.400
We can go now if you want.

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:30.540
Wait a moment.

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:36.510
You're still going to help people from the air raids?

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:38.140
Yeah, that's right.

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:41.150
Listen to me, Arashi.

00:09:41.150 --> 00:09:45.720
Have you ever thought about how you affect the present by altering the past?

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.760
You might change history.

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:54.130
But even you were happy to be able to tell the master you loved him, right?

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:56.190
I didn't do it!

00:09:56.190 --> 00:09:58.040
What? You didn't?

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:00.360
Why are you getting involved all of a sudden?

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:04.210
No real reason. I mostly ignored you because it was all about the past and future,

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:06.760
and all this stuff I didn't understand.

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:09.540
But if love's involved, that's different. That's interesting.

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:11.500
It is not!

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:13.910
Wait, you didn't tell him you liked him?

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:15.760
Of course I didn't!

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:18.800
If I did, history would...

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:25.850
And time passes, huh?

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:28.150
Um... Salt?

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:34.090
Jun?

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:41.780
Manami-san, Saki-san, Youko!

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:43.860
What are you doing around here?

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:45.560
And what's with that outfit?

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:46.740
It's so cool!

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:48.160
It's for a job or something?

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:50.850
You sure it's OK? Shouldn't you go through the agency?

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:53.250
No, this is...

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:58.810
Oh, I see. So that's what happened.

00:10:58.810 --> 00:11:00.650
But I'm amazed they haven't figured it out.

00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:03.840
She has a husky voice. Maybe she'll be OK.

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:10.850
But you know, I think you should dress up a little more womanly, Jun.

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:15.170
At the last group date, you were wearing jeans.

00:11:15.170 --> 00:11:18.520
And you left halfway through.

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:21.080
You left just before it got good.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:24.650
And there was a guy who said he was interested in you.

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:26.110
Really?

00:11:26.770 --> 00:11:29.120
See, this feeling again...

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:34.370
It was such a waste, wasn't it?

00:11:34.370 --> 00:11:35.490
Yeah.

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:36.880
It's women...

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:38.730
I hate them.

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:42.120
Am I gonna end up like this someday?

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:42.810
Jun?

00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:51.020
Kaya-san?

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:52.780
How did you find me?

00:11:52.780 --> 00:11:55.440
Don't underestimate the person you connected with.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:58.480
What are you doing in a place like this?

00:11:58.480 --> 00:11:59.620
Weren't you going shopping?

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:01.920
Wow, she's so pretty.

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:02.540
Who's she?

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:03.500
A friend of Jun's?

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:08.010
This is Kaya-san. She works at the coffee shop I was telling you about.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:10.810
Her name's Kaya-san?

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:11.970
Are these your friends?

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:13.080
They seem lively.

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:16.820
Um, they're fellow models.

00:12:16.820 --> 00:12:18.840
That kimono looks really good on you.

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:22.220
Kaya-san, what country are you from?

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:24.330
Um, Germany.

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:27.550
You look really Japanese.

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:32.420
Your posture is great, just like my Japanese dance teacher's!

00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:35.100
Like an old-fashioned, proper Japanese lady.

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:37.130
Y-You think so?

00:12:37.130 --> 00:12:40.100
I wish I were like that...

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:41.360
Japanese dance, huh?

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:45.080
That brings back memories. It's still being done?

00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:48.050
You can do that?

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:50.450
Yes, at an amateur level.

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:53.020
What style?

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:54.390
I'd like to see it!

00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:54.960
Yeah!

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:56.230
Me too! Me too!

00:12:56.230 --> 00:12:57.500
Wait, everyone-

00:12:57.500 --> 00:12:58.320
All right.

00:12:58.810 --> 00:13:00.150
Just a bit...

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:01.870
All right!

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:02.880
Are you sure?

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:05.600
Then...

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:05.360
Wow!

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:06.960
You're so pretty, Kaya-san!

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:10.960
Is there anything else you can do?

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:13.830
Hm, let's see... The tea ceremony, maybe...

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:16.090
We're learning that, too!

00:14:16.090 --> 00:14:18.480
Can we see a bit of that?

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:19.490
Please!

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:21.290
Jun.

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:23.750
These girls have a lot of promise.

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:29.510
I guess I already knew, but it's pretty easy to get Kaya-san to do what you want.

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:31.990
Kaya-san, quickly. Quickly!

00:14:31.990 --> 00:14:32.650
Yes.

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:34.880
Oh, I guess they're here.

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:36.270
This way. This way!

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:39.200
Hey, guys.

00:14:40.590 --> 00:14:42.830
Good to see you, Tera-sempai!

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:44.050
What is this, girls?

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:47.370
We've got a group date today.

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:48.430
A group date?

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:50.730
Why don't you join us, Kaya-san?

00:14:52.470 --> 00:14:54.480
But you'll probably get them all.

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:55.830
Yeah!

00:14:57.230 --> 00:14:58.080
What?

00:14:58.080 --> 00:14:59.390
Cute!

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:00.750
You guys got a foreign girl?

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:02.990
What's your name?

00:15:06.190 --> 00:15:08.500
Ah, I... I...

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:10.210
Kaya-san?

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:12.960
I-I have something I must do!

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:13.930
Goodbye!

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:20.990
Kaya-san?

00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:28.040
Hey, Master.

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:29.010
Where's Kaya-san?

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:32.450
She said that Jun was taking a while and left.

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:37.770
Dunno if she feels responsible or what, but she wants to help him out.

00:15:38.770 --> 00:15:40.450
Anyway, this...

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:42.520
You did it.

00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:44.430
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:46.800
You break it,

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:48.190
you buy it.

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:54.550
Damn it, who would do that?

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:57.000
Oh, sorry, Hajime-chan.

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:58.300
That was me.

00:15:59.210 --> 00:16:03.090
You know, you should put your name on your things, right?

00:16:03.090 --> 00:16:05.040
It'd suck if you lost them.

00:16:11.670 --> 00:16:13.820
I had no idea there was more listed on the back...

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:14.820
Damn it.

00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:23.710
Welcome!

00:16:24.740 --> 00:16:26.540
Did you forget something?

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:31.250
Um, well... It's not for me, but...

00:16:31.250 --> 00:16:36.090
I'd like a well-fitted, secret miracle b-b-b-

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:37.340
Brassiere?

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:38.170
Yes.

00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:50.740
Are you OK?

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:59.480
In my time, contact between boys and girls was strictly forbidden.

00:17:00.270 --> 00:17:02.730
Giving someone a love letter was grounds for expulsion.

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:06.880
Students were yelled at for simply walking together.

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.680
That's right...

00:17:09.010 --> 00:17:11.760
I was taught to be chaste and virtuous, to avoid men.

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:15.500
And I think that that's right.

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:16.270
For...

00:17:16.850 --> 00:17:21.270
Loving someone should be your whole life.

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:26.060
What truth and joy is there in love that can be redone?

00:17:26.490 --> 00:17:33.060
Kaya lives exactly opposite to how my sister and the models around me do.

00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:38.330
The mysterious hatred I feel towards them...

00:17:40.420 --> 00:17:45.000
The feeling that someday,
I may become like them-I hate it.

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:53.580
But living in this era, I sometimes find myself feeling very small and pathetic for thinking that.

00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:58.310
Love truly does drive people mad...

00:18:00.190 --> 00:18:02.550
I can't believe I made you go through that.

00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:04.560
I'm sorry.

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:15.490
I shouldn't go see him, should I?

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:17.790
He's going to die anyway.

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:21.660
To think only of another...

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:27.470
To think of them far too much, so you just curl yourself into a ball and shake...

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:33.240
We simply got caught in the blast from a bomb dropped in an air raid.

00:18:33.240 --> 00:18:36.220
There's no meaning to this body, no purpose.

00:18:39.310 --> 00:18:41.500
We repeat the summer over and over again.

00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:45.050
And perhaps someday, we'll just disappear.

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:47.470
You loved him, didn't you?

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:54.160
Kaya-san, you're just a coward.

00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:57.490
It's not history you're afraid of destroying. It's yourself!

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:05.580
The person you loved died in the war before you could tell him how you felt.

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:09.340
You were overwhelmed with regret. That's why you're here!

00:19:11.530 --> 00:19:14.490
If you won't say it now, when will you?

00:19:14.490 --> 00:19:17.630
Tell him you love him with everything you've got!

00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:19.100
Scream it out!

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:22.290
That's why you're alive.

00:19:30.680 --> 00:19:31.610
You're right.

00:19:50.880 --> 00:19:52.680
Look. Look, Hajime-chan!

00:19:52.680 --> 00:19:54.290
Wow! A rainbow!

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:55.180
Awesome!

00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:57.840
I won't lose!

00:20:02.810 --> 00:20:05.150
Nice, Hajime-chan!

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:07.680
Hey, Hajime-chan...

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:11.400
When they get back, let's show Kaya and Jun this rainbow.

00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:12.770
Of course!

00:20:25.380 --> 00:20:27.570
I had no idea that it was sold separately.

00:20:30.990 --> 00:20:33.900
Women put these things in?

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:36.420
It's fraud, I tell you.

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:37.430
Sir.

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:38.970
Is there something else?

00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:40.310
No, no, no!

00:20:40.310 --> 00:20:41.690
It's not for me.

00:20:41.690 --> 00:20:42.880
But these!

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:44.020
Pads.

00:20:44.020 --> 00:20:45.340
All right, one moment.

00:20:45.710 --> 00:20:50.150
Ah, can I get a receipt for all that?

00:20:50.150 --> 00:20:51.330
I'm sorry?

00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:53.760
They aren't for me.

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:55.960
To Be Continued

00:22:28.950 --> 00:22:30.910
How are you today, Yayoi?

00:22:31.210 --> 00:22:33.200
I'm very good, Kanako.

00:22:33.560 --> 00:22:35.750
I see. I'm happy to hear that.

00:22:36.030 --> 00:22:38.640
I read another fascinating book.

00:22:38.640 --> 00:22:41.730
My, what was it called?

00:22:41.730 --> 00:22:45.380
Well... Oh, I've forgotten the title.

00:22:45.640 --> 00:22:47.840
Will you tell me what kind of story it was?

00:22:48.150 --> 00:22:50.110
Yes, gladly.

00:22:52.370 --> 00:22:57.000
It was the beautiful, dazzling story of a young child.

00:22:57.000 --> 00:23:01.350
The pearl, diamond, jade, and gold hidden within him

00:23:01.350 --> 00:23:06.720
enchant all he meets, and the troubles they attract are endless.

00:23:06.720 --> 00:23:11.040
The words from his pure, unsullied heart and the smile

00:23:11.040 --> 00:23:15.110
of the young heir have an unmistakable and unique effect on his friends.

00:23:15.840 --> 00:23:19.070
My, what a dazzling story.

00:23:19.590 --> 00:23:24.100
This blessed heir had a phrase he would always say.

00:23:24.100 --> 00:23:26.000
What is it? Would you tell <i>me?</i>

00:23:28.010 --> 00:23:28.960
<i>Fwiends-</i>

00:23:31.230 --> 00:23:32.530
When you think of summer-

00:23:32.530 --> 00:23:33.810
You think of fuurin-wind chimes!

00:23:33.810 --> 00:23:40.310
As fast as the wind, quiet as the forest,
daring as fire, and immovable as the mountain!

00:23:40.310 --> 00:23:41.960
That's Fuurin Kazan, a TV show.

00:23:41.960 --> 00:23:44.950
Get up bright and early tomorrow!

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:50.450
<i>Get up bright and early tomorrow!</i>

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:50.450
Illustration by Takeshi Fujishiro
